Package: ssh3-client
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5)
Conflicts: ssh3-go-client
Replaces: ssh3-go-client
Description: SSH3 client - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 SSH3 client: sessions, the ssh(1)-canon forwards (-L/-R/-D with the
 udp:// extension), -J proxy jumps, the control master (-M/-S/-O),
 the agent forwarding (-A), file transfers (put|get) and the
 in-process sftp subsystem, all over one HTTP/3 (QUIC) extended
 CONNECT per target.
 .
 The CLI follows the ssh(1) canon: -4/-6, -e escape, -F ssh_config
 (HostName, Port, User, IdentityFile, ForwardAgent, the forwards,
 ProxyJump, StrictHostKeyChecking, ControlMaster/Path/Persist), -o
 keyword overrides, -t/-T pty control, -V.
 The first connection pins the server certificate TOFU-style in
 ~/.ssh3/known_hosts (the same store the go implementation reads).
 See ssh3(1).

Package: ssh3-server
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5),
 adduser,
 ssh3-client (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: ssh3-go-server
Replaces: ssh3-go-server
Description: SSH3 server - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 SSH3 server daemon: the SSH3 protocol carried over HTTP/3 (QUIC),
 implemented in C17 in the nginx style on top of the OpenSSL QUIC TLS
 API (the system libssl3t64, 3.5+).
 .
 The UDP/443 QUIC listener is socket-activated: systemd binds the
 datagram socket as root and hands the ready fd to the service
 (sd_listen_fds), so the service needs no CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE and
 comes up on the first packet.
 .
 System accounts authenticate out of the box: the password login
 rides on by default (the sshd PasswordAuthentication canon) and the
 root account never passes the Basic step.  Bearer JWT public keys,
 OIDC id_tokens, sessions, port forwarding and the in-process sftp
 with a chroot jail are also supported.
 .
 The daemon is configured through command-line flags (ssh3-server
 --help) and environment variables read from the conffile
 /etc/ssh3/ssh3-server.env (SSH3_LOG_LEVEL, SSH3_LOG_FILE,
 SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN, SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN).  See
 ssh3-server(8).
 .
 The server depends on the matching ssh3-client (the openssh(8)
 canon: one release wave ships both halves together).

Package: ssh3c
Architecture: all
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ssh3-client,
 ssh3-server
Description: SSH3 - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 (client and server metapackage)
 The openssh(8) `ssh' metapackage analog of this source package:
 installs the ssh3-client and ssh3-server packages at matching
 versions, so one install brings up the full SSH3 pair - the client
 CLI and the socket-activated server daemon.
